+# VPP2 IKV inference modes
+
+This implementation lives on server `.239` in
+`${IKV_DEPLOY_ROOT}/video-prediction-policy-2`.
+It uses the sibling `ikv_runtime` package; it does not use a local checkout.
+
+| `history_mode` | RGB encoded for policy inference each replan | KV consumed by Action |
+|---|---|---|
+| `off` (default) | Native anchor plus history8 | Native freshly computed video cache |
+| `window_refresh` | Same native nine-frame window | Scorer-selected real historical/current KV replaces the three condition slots |
+| `incremental_reuse` | Current three-camera observation only | New current KV joins the entire archive; scorer selects the same three-slot budget |
+
+For 240x416 input the condition budget is 1,170 KV tokens per layer.
+The 780 future-video KV tokens are always computed in the current request.
+The action-visible cache therefore keeps 1,950 video tokens. Empty warmup
+memory positions are zero padded and masked, never fabricated as observations.
+
+## Configuration
+
+Merge `configs/robodojo/ikv_example.yaml` into the arguments passed to
+`RoboDojoVPP2Policy` / `get_model`. Supply real scorer source, checkpoint and
+encoder paths. All three are required: there is no recency/random fallback.
+The production environment must provide the scorer's Qwen3.5-compatible
+Transformers/encoder dependencies. The existing runtime310 environment used
+for CPU adapter tests has Transformers 4.57 and is not sufficient to load the
+real Qwen3.5 encoder by itself. A validated server-only overlay is now available
+at `${IKV_DEPLOY_ROOT}/scorer-test-deps`: Transformers
+5.14.1, huggingface-hub 1.5.0 and safetensors 0.8.0. It leaves the shared
+runtime unchanged. The scorer uses its own 0.8B encoder; it does not silently reuse the policy VAE.
+
+Set the import path before launching the existing policy runner:
+
+```sh
+export PYTHONPATH=${IKV_DEPLOY_ROOT}/scorer-test-deps:${IKV_DEPLOY_ROOT}/test-deps:${IKV_DEPLOY_ROOT}:${IKV_DEPLOY_ROOT}/video-prediction-policy-2/src
+```
+
+The side-chat/DM05 spelling `incremental` is accepted as an alias for
+`incremental_reuse`. Unlike DM05's common per-frame representation, these
+VPP2 modes construct different temporal candidates, so changing modes requires
+an episode reset.
+
+The modes can be changed through `set_history_mode(...)` only after resetting
+all environments. `reset_env(i)` clears only that environment's archive,
+scorer features and anchor CLIP cache. Scorer forks share frozen model weights
+and keep separate observation features.
+
+## What is computed
+
+`window_refresh` preserves the native Video forward. Per-layer normalized keys
+are captured directly before RoPE for archival; the selected keys are rotated into the existing
+condition positions before Action reads them. If the complete fresh window
+is selected in place, the original native cache tensors are used exactly.
+
+`incremental_reuse` keeps the native five-latent noise draw so the future
+slots retain their original random samples. It places the independently
+encoded current observation at native condition slot 2, then evaluates only
+slot 2 and future slots 3/4 as Transformer queries. Slots 0/1 contain no
+historical RGB input and are not Transformer queries. At every layer, selected
+archived/current keys and values plus fresh future keys and values form the
+attention key side. A rectangular mask accounts for the smaller query side.
+The same selected plan is used by all layers and the Action branch sees it
+from its first denoising step.
+
+The episode-first CLIP features are computed once and reused. They retain
+the native anchor conditioning without re-encoding historical RGB each round.
+
+KV keys are real model attention keys, not image embeddings. The bank stores
+all candidates, including candidates not selected this round. Its configured
+CPU byte limit raises an error before publishing a new archive rather than
+silently evicting candidates. The archive commits only after inference yields
+finite, correctly shaped actions; exceptions abort staged KV.
+
+## Limits and interpretation
+
+This is a new inference algorithm, not an equivalence claim for the native
+bidirectional Video transformer. Archived KV retain their old context and
+noise dependence. Single-frame VAE encoding also differs from the original
+nine-frame temporal VAE input. Check performance against `off` and
+`window_refresh` using the same seeds and task splits.
+
+Scorer regions map the resized T-shaped grid back to head/left-wrist/right-wrist
+camera rectangles. A native temporal latent's nominal group of RGB sources is
+used for score mapping; this is not an exact VAE receptive-field inversion.
+Source slot is part of candidate identity, so padded warmup groups remain
+distinct even when all RGB source timestamps are zero.
+
+The initial implementation supports batch 1 per call, direct per-layer Video
+KV, five video latents and bidirectional video attention. It rejects alternate
+first-frame routes, fixed/shared source layers, token-projection cache modes
+and diagnostic video generation. PP is a separate deployment adaptation.
+
+## Verification
+
+The CPU tests execute actual small MoT/DiT blocks without model weights:
+
+```sh
+cd ${IKV_DEPLOY_ROOT}/video-prediction-policy-2
+PYTHONPATH=${IKV_DEPLOY_ROOT}/scorer-test-deps:${IKV_DEPLOY_ROOT}/test-deps:${IKV_DEPLOY_ROOT}:src \
+  python \
+  -m unittest discover -s tests -v
+```
+
+They cover warmup identity, native-cache bitwise parity when all fresh KV are
+selected, old-KV retrieval, current/future query and cache lengths, camera-region
+mapping, RoPE relocation, abort and environment isolation. Full checkpoint GPU
+inference and RoboDojo success-rate evaluation remain to be run.
+
+
+Incremental warmup keeps real memory at the right end of the three-latent
+condition prefix. With one observed frame, its keys and queries both use native
+temporal slot 2; with two frames, their memory occupies slots 1 and 2. Empty
+earlier slots are zero and masked. This only places padding: it does not protect
+any candidate from scoring, change the memory budget, or move the two freshly
+computed future-video slots. The shared CPU archive remains independent of this
+VPP2 consumer layout.
+
+The independent **real** Qwen3.5 encoder and trained 10.9M SFT scorer were also
+validated on the server's 4090, using two synthetic RGB observations. Image
+features were encoded once per observation, repeated task scoring reused its
+text features, and new subtask/memory feedback triggered a new text encoding.
+Both the model SHA and the `:linear-patch-v1` contract were checked.
+
+Evidence and the exact isolated environment are stored on `.239`:
+
+- `${IKV_DEPLOY_ROOT}/REAL_ENCODER_SMOKE.json`
+- `${IKV_DEPLOY_ROOT}/validation-assets/SCORER_VALIDATION_ENV.json`
+
+This validates the actual scorer/encoder bridge. Full VPP2 checkpoint GPU
+inference, PP deployment and RoboDojo success-rate evaluation are separate
+remaining checks.
+
+
+## Canonical heuristic inference
+
+Set `ikv.backend: formula`, with `source_root` pointing to the current IKV
+core and `encoder_path` to verified raw DINOv3 assets. The new formula is the
+un-normalized sum of recency, visual contact decay and prototype-gated class
+recency, all weights one, threshold 0.75, decay 8 world/control steps. There
+is no random mixture. The bridge converts adapter seconds back to world steps
+explicitly (VPP2: 25 Hz; HWM: native control clock). DINO uses its own frozen
+encoder and maps its 14x14 scores to native KV provenance by area and temporal
+support. It does not share the Planner encoder.
+
+Native RGB-only requests have no contact-duration sidecar; their absent-contact
+value is d=0. The bridge accepts validated per-sensor contact durations (world
+steps) when a caller supplies them; it never guesses contact from RGB.
+Formula scoring has no instruction/subtask/semantic-memory term, so HWM formula
+runs require `planner_mode: lower_only`. Native Planner still runs normally.
+The learned backend retains its independent `interactive` option. Both history
+update modes remain available for formula runs. Feature caching and class-index
+reuse are episode-local and use only causal real observations. Prototype overflow
+fails explicitly rather than silently evicting classes.
